          <h2>Artefact: Air BnB Team Project</h2>
          <p>Machine Learning Team Project .</p>
        </header>

        <section>
          <h3>Overview</h3>
          <p>This artefact documents my contribution to a collaborative Airbnb business analysis project (Classical Machine Learning – Regression and Clustering).  
             The project used the 2019 New York City Airbnb dataset to investigate how regression models and clustering techniques could support listing price 
             prediction and neighbourhood market segmentation.  My individual contribution focused on evaluating the business implications of these approaches, 
             particularly their potential to improve pricing strategies, revenue forecasting, host profitability and targeted business decisions.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h3>My Contribution- Business Implications</h3>
          <p>The price prediction and neighbourhood segmentation outputs generate several actionable insights for Airbnb’s strategic decision making around pricing 
             and host support in the NYC market.  Predictive pricing enhances revenue forecasting accuracy by estimating expected listing values based on observable 
             property and location attributes.</p>

          <p>Accurate forecasts help align host pricing behaviour with actual demand, reducing revenue leakage from underpricing and improving host profitability 
             (Zervas et al., 2017).  This also enables Airbnb to refine commission forecasts, supporting strategic financial planning.</p>
          
          <p>Market segmentation uncovers customer and listing clusters, allowing Airbnb to tailor pricing strategies and platform support services.  For example, 
             segmentation can differentiate premium urban core listings from mid range or budget listings in outer boroughs, enabling targeted pricing recommendations 
             and service tiering.  Research shows that segmenting by location and amenities reveals commercially distinct market groups with different pricing and 
             demand characteristics (Guttentag, 2013).  By tailoring pricing guidance, visibility tools and marketing incentives to segment specific characteristics, 
             Airbnb can allocate promotional spend more efficiently, maximising returns across neighbourhood markets.</p>
          
          <p>Combining regression based price prediction with clustering enhances operational decisions by enabling neighbourhood level pricing guidance and 
             differentiated host support, while maintaining model interpretability, a requirement for platform governance and host adoption (Einav et al., 2016).  
             Interpretable analytics allow Airbnb to justify pricing to hosts, reinforcing trust and compliance.  This classical ML approach translates into actionable 
             strategic levers including: targeted pricing, segment specific incentives, and more predictable revenue outcomes, strengthening competitive positioning 
             in one of Airbnb’s most data rich markets.</p>

